**Location:** src/ast/expressions.rs:73-173

**Problem:** The `Expr::AstNode` implementation has 27 match arms repeated three times (`can_cast`, `cast`, `syntax`). This is error-prone when adding new variants.

**Example of duplication:**
```rust
impl AstNode for Expr {
    fn can_cast(kind: SyntaxKind) -> bool {
        match kind {
            SyntaxKind::LITERAL_EXPR => true,
            SyntaxKind::PATH_EXPR => true,
            // ... 25 more variants
        }
    }

    fn cast(node: SyntaxNode) -> Option<Self> {
        match node.kind() {
            SyntaxKind::LITERAL_EXPR => Some(Expr::Literal(LiteralExpr(node))),
            // ... same 27 variants again
        }
    }

    fn syntax(&self) -> &SyntaxNode {
        match self {
            Expr::Literal(it) => &it.0,
            // ... same 27 variants again
        }
    }
}
```

**Fix:** Consider a procedural macro or extending the `ast_node!` macro to generate enum wrapper implementations automatically, similar to rust-analyzer's `ungrammar` approach.

**Severity:** Minor - maintenance burden, error-prone when adding variants

